# Inbox — raw research ideas (human scratchpad)

Drop ideas here the moment they occur — half-formed is fine, no format
police. One `- ` bullet per idea (indented lines continue the same idea).
Prose outside bullets is ignored by tooling, so you can annotate freely.

An agent formalizes entries into [`ROADMAP.md`](ROADMAP.md) on request
("sweep the experiments inbox"): complete ideas move straight over, and
for incomplete ones the agent asks targeted questions (expected payoff?
research or engineering? which findings does it assume?) instead of
guessing. Swept bullets are deleted; the idea lives on in the ROADMAP.

Optional inline hints, if you already know them (quotes allowed):
`lane=P2 effort=M cat=research payoff="decides go/no-go on X" depends-on=F-003 title="..."`

